        "original_id": "198f5707-d6ac-54ed-9100-24b555eef0b2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Dear America book series\n- Events: Triangle Shirtwaist Factory fire\n- People: Patricia McKissack\n- Topics: American history topics in Dear America\n\nFacts:\n- The Dear America series covers many American history topics, including the Pilgrims' journey to the New World, the Salem Witch Trials, the French and Indian War, the American Revolution, the American Civil War, World War I, World War II, western expansion, slavery, immigration, prairie life, the California Gold Rush, the Great Depression, Native American experiences, racism, coal mining, the Triangle Shirtwaist Factory fire, women's suffrage, the sinking of the RMS Titanic, the Battle of the Alamo, and the Vietnam War.\n- The Triangle Shirtwaist Factory fire occurred in New York City on March 25, 1911.\n- The Triangle Shirtwaist Factory fire was the deadliest industrial disaster in New York City history and one of the deadliest industrial disasters in United States history.\n- Patricia McKissack wrote Dear America books including A Picture of Freedom: The Diary of Clotee, a Slave Girl, Color Me Dark: The Diary of Nellie Lee Love, The Great Migration North, and Look to the Hills: The Diary of Lozette Moreau, a French Slave Girl.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "cf26ffcd-a892-5386-b4b3-b9bf65c2a4be",
        "text": "Page: Dear America. Sentence: The Dear America series covers a wide range of topics, including: the Pilgrims' journey to the New World, the Salem Witch Trials, the French and Indian War, the American Revolution, the American Civil War, World War I, World War II, western expansion, slavery, immigration, nineteenth-century prairie life, the California Gold Rush of 1849, the Great Depression, Native Americans' experiences, racism, coal mining, the Triangle Shirtwaist Factory fire, the fight for women's suffrage, the sinking of the RMS \"Titanic\", the Battle of the Alamo, the Vietnam War, and more.\nPage: Triangle Shirtwaist Factory fire. Sentence: The Triangle Shirtwaist Factory fire in New York City on March 25, 1911 was the deadliest industrial disaster in the history of the city, and one of the deadliest in US history.\nPage: Patricia McKissack. Sentence: She was the author of three \"Dear America\" books: \"A Picture of Freedom: The Diary of Clotee, a Slave Girl\", \"Color Me Dark: The Diary of Nellie Lee Love\", \"The Great Migration North\", and \"Look to the Hills: The Diary of Lozette Moreau, a French Slave Girl\".",
